cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  Cite the software snapshot using this metadata and its exact commit or tag.
  Cite the original papers separately when using their methods. This repository
  is research software, not a published validation study of measured fabrics.
type: software
title: Multiscale Textile Appearance Modeling and Meta-Optical Sensing
version: 0.5.0
authors:
  - name: Phill-lms
repository-code: https://github.com/Phill-lms/textile-appearance-research
abstract: >-
  Research software for reducing the gap between textile appearance on screens
  and in person through multiscale physics, computational imaging and
  experimentally justified meta-optical sensing. It includes an explicit
  fiber-to-ply-to-yarn-to-woven-fabric engine with
  versioned geometry, constituent optical spectra, validated local 2D wave
  and ray adapters, reduced quasi-static yarn-height equilibrium, hierarchical
  projected-area and SGGX diagnostics, and multi-material explicit-fiber spectral
  path tracing with CIE observation, and fixed-reference yarn-to-ply-to-fiber
  material-coordinate transport with local strain and segment cylinder-volume
  diagnostics. Variable-radius profiles are connected to closed triangle meshes,
  real-index dielectric boundaries and physical path-length absorption, with
  explicit tessellation, unit-scale and Monte Carlo uncertainty diagnostics.
  Developed under user direction with AI assistance. Current examples use
  synthetic materials and prescribed kinematic correspondence. Variable-radius
  reconstruction preserves a per-fiber frustum integral, not local physical mass.
  Full rod/contact mechanics, aggregate fabric BSDFs,
  measured-fabric fidelity, and metasurface sensing remain separate research tasks.
keywords:
  - computational imaging
  - textile microgeometry
  - woven fabric
  - fiber scattering
  - optical simulation
  - reduced yarn mechanics
  - material coordinates
  - spectral rendering
  - reproducible simulation
  - research software
